// What the cosigner needs from the runtime it runs inside.
//
// Its own world, rather than an edited copy of `enclave:tasks`'s: the vendored `tasks.wit` and
// `notify.wit` under `deps/` are byte-for-byte copies of the canonical ones in
// `~/enclave-runtime/wit/`, and `scripts/wit-drift.sh` checks that they stay that way. A guest that
// wants two capabilities composes them here instead of editing either.
//
// Not yet generated from. The crate now builds as a wasm32-wasip2 component — `make cosigner-wasm`
// — serving gRPC over `wasi:http/incoming-handler`, which removed the reason this could not be
// generated. What remains is composing this world with the one `wstd::http_server` exports, so
// `src/host.rs` still mirrors these signatures behind a trait and `tests/wit_test.rs` checks the
// mirror against this file. Wiring `wit_bindgen::generate!` over this world replaces the trait's
// `Detached` impl and is the last step.
package merlin:cosigner@0.1.0;

world cosigner {
    // `run-task`, plus the queue to arm it with. The cosigner uses this for one thing: a settle
    // that has come due. Where the image allowlists the ASP the task executes the sealed delegate
    // itself; where it does not, it reads the delegate, compares the deadline to the clock, and
    // wakes its owner instead. Egress is the image's to grant, and is not named in this world.
    include enclave:tasks/background@0.1.0;

    // Waking those devices. The cosigner never sees a token and never sends a message; it spends
    // an enrolment an interactive call already made.
    import enclave:notify/notify@0.1.0;

    // A connection the RUNTIME holds to an escrow service, and the messages that arrive on it.
    //
    // The cosigner cannot hold one itself: it has no execution context between invocations, so
    // there is nothing for a socket to belong to. And it needs one, because a service holding half
    // of an escrow key has no passkey for its user's tenant and so can never call in. The runtime
    // keeps the connection; each message the service sends becomes one invocation of `on-message`,
    // exactly as a due task becomes one invocation of `run-task`.
    include enclave:streams/streaming@0.1.0;
}
